# Quest book (design/quests/*.toml → tools/gen_quests.py → pack/config/ftbquests/quests/) and the Life 1 extras
# in kubejs/server_scripts/ttl/quests/. `ttl quests ...` prints "ttl: ..." on any failure, which
# `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure.
# Expect in the log: no "[ttl] quests" errors; the bot hears "One day and one night." once.
# 1. Every generated chapter and quest is loaded by FTB Quests.
ttl quests check
# 2. A fresh Life 1 gets the Wayfarer's Primer and no backlog of whispers.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotQuests
# A bot left over from an earlier run may already be past Life 1: start it fresh.
ttl reset TtlBotQuests
@sleep 8
ttl quests tick TtlBotQuests
ttl quests expect TtlBotQuests primer yes
# 3. Surviving the first day earns exactly one whisper.
ttl karma TtlBotQuests set play_time 24000
ttl quests tick TtlBotQuests
ttl quests expect TtlBotQuests said day1
# 4. FTB Quests accepts the bot: complete and reset the first quest ("Only Once", id from generated/quests.js).
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotQuests complete 50382544FBB449E8
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotQuests reset 50382544FBB449E8
ttlbot remove TtlBotQuests
# 5. Story chapters 7 (Crossroads) and 8 (The King's Test): tools/gen_quests.py story extensions in use (design/quests.md, WP-S6).
# `ttl quests check` above already proves that every chapter-7/8 quest loaded, including the cross-chapter `deps`
# (FTB Quests drops an unresolved dependency silently, so a quest missing from the check is the symptom).
# There is no command that claims a reward or reads quest visibility, so the flows below do what the book does: complete the quest
# through FTB (`ftbquests change_progress`, which auto-claims the invisible rewards: the honour flag) and run the claimed command
# reward as the bot (`ttl story oath|act|fight`, the same commands the reward lines run). NOT asserted here, verify in game:
# a dark soul never sees the light lane (and the reverse), the Oath menu opens from the Crossroads reward, a party shares the lane.
# ids are from generated/quests.js: crossroads/crossroads 3D14EC5F5890B8B5, kings_test/honour_terms 5CE177F176862D46,
# kings_test/regicide 6A02570FD1A84087, kings_test/act_two 6DDF459E16D36563.
# L: the light lane. The Oath (the Crossroads reward), then "Terms of Honour" sets honour_duel by itself, the kill then costs nothing.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLaneL
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLaneD
@sleep 2
ttl reset TtlBotLaneL
ttl reset TtlBotLaneD
kubejs stages add TtlBotLaneL ttl.life2
kubejs stages add TtlBotLaneD ttl.life2
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneL reset 3D14EC5F5890B8B5
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneL reset 5CE177F176862D46
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneD reset 3D14EC5F5890B8B5
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneD reset 6A02570FD1A84087
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneL complete 3D14EC5F5890B8B5
execute as TtlBotLaneL run ttl story oath light
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL path light
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL stage ttl.path.light yes
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL stage ttl.story.act1 yes
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL flag honour_duel no
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneL complete 5CE177F176862D46
@sleep 2
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL flag honour_duel yes
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL stage ttl.story.honour_duel yes
ttl story killrep TtlBotLaneL gazel_dwargo
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL flag honour_duel no
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL flag regicide no
ttl rep expect TtlBotLaneL dwargon value 0
ttl story act TtlBotLaneL 2
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneL act 2 yes
ttl rep expect TtlBotLaneL dwargon value 15
# D: the dark lane. Regicide (no honour flag): Dwargon -60 and the flag, then Act II by the finale's reward (-20 more, Outcast +10).
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneD complete 3D14EC5F5890B8B5
execute as TtlBotLaneD run ttl story oath dark
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneD path dark
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneD stage ttl.path.dark yes
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneD flag honour_duel no
ttl story killrep TtlBotLaneD gazel_dwargo
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneD flag regicide yes
ttl rep expect TtlBotLaneD dwargon value -60
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneD complete 6A02570FD1A84087
ttl story act TtlBotLaneD 2
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneD act 2 yes
ttl rep expect TtlBotLaneD dwargon value -80
ttl story expect TtlBotLaneD flag honour_duel no
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneL reset 3D14EC5F5890B8B5
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneL reset 5CE177F176862D46
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneD reset 3D14EC5F5890B8B5
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotLaneD reset 6A02570FD1A84087
ttl reset TtlBotLaneL
ttl reset TtlBotLaneD
ttlbot remove TtlBotLaneL
ttlbot remove TtlBotLaneD
# 6. The quest web (design/quests.md "The web", WP quests-web): the entry points of the ten new Life 1 chapters and of the quests the web
# re-wired (Life 2 story order, dailies) are accepted by FTB Quests. `ttl quests check` (step 1) already proves every generated quest loaded,
# including every cross-chapter dep (an unresolved one is dropped silently, so a quest missing from the check is the symptom); the offline test
# tests/test_gen_quests.py (QuestWebTests) proves the graph itself (every quest unlockable, one connected web, Life 1 converging on its finale,
# Life 2 order). There is no command that reads quest visibility, so what a player SEES (the new Life 1 chapters unlocking one after another, the
# nether and end chapters hidden until the portal and the stronghold quests are done, dailies appearing after the first night or the first visit to
# Tempest) is NOT asserted here: verify in game. ids are from generated/quests.js.
# first_days/bare_hands 283DBEA71CB9C9E6, first_days/ready_for_road 522F16F19507224C, homestead/hearth 219098709232BE9A,
# fields/first_seeds 0BA57A81D13A7783, delving/coal_seam 0B48B9D221810B49, roads_ruins/long_walker 40A33D79BFA6EAAC, folk/ring_bell 1D03190909C19A0D,
# arts/scribe 443CA0DC588BEC52, nether_road/first_footing 70EB5B4005F7C8E2, end_road/apples_of_gold 177FAA70EB81D656,
# a_life_that_counts/ledger 51BE6D1FFA78B4AF, a_life_that_counts/legend 5557926F5E401552, reborn/tempest 27035168A6DEED93,
# tempest_rises/join_town 63A48763F37F8D6C, armed_nation/road_supplies 16C682117AAF591D, orc_lord/envoy 72ED01B72020F604,
# daily_deeds/hunt_zombies 33FCE563EA7EA5CF, daily_jura/jura_patrol 4895991B15F57CD2.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotWeb
@sleep 2
ttl reset TtlBotWeb
kubejs stages add TtlBotWeb ttl.life1
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 283DBEA71CB9C9E6
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 522F16F19507224C
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 219098709232BE9A
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 0BA57A81D13A7783
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 0B48B9D221810B49
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 40A33D79BFA6EAAC
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 1D03190909C19A0D
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 443CA0DC588BEC52
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 70EB5B4005F7C8E2
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 177FAA70EB81D656
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 51BE6D1FFA78B4AF
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 5557926F5E401552
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 27035168A6DEED93
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 63A48763F37F8D6C
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 16C682117AAF591D
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 72ED01B72020F604
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 33FCE563EA7EA5CF
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 4895991B15F57CD2
# Complete a few of them the way a player would (force-completing skips the dependency check, as for the story chapters above), then clear them.
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb complete 283DBEA71CB9C9E6
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb complete 522F16F19507224C
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb complete 5557926F5E401552
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 283DBEA71CB9C9E6
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 522F16F19507224C
ftbquests change_progress TtlBotWeb reset 5557926F5E401552
ttl reset TtlBotWeb
ttlbot remove TtlBotWeb
